\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Y-Statement is a highly structured, single-sentence template used to capture the core architectural decision quickly. It gets its name because its visual architecture or structural flow resembles the letter "Y"\'97branching out from a context into a choice, a rationale, and the resulting trade-offs.\
It was popularized by software architect Olaf Zimmermann to help teams document decisions in a fast, punchy, and standardized way without writing pages of documentation.\
\
