\f2\i\b\fs36 ## A Concrete Example\
\pard\tx0\tx0\tx567\tx1134\tx1701\sl312\slmult1\pardirnatural\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\i0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2><!$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0 Here is how a real-world decision looks when mapped to a Y-Statement:\
\
In the context of our new e-commerce microservices,\
we faced the challenge of choosing a reliable data storage for shopping carts.\
We decided on Redis,\
and neglected PostgreSQL and DynamoDB,\
to achieve sub-millisecond read/write speeds and automatic session expiration,\
accepting the risk of data loss if the cache node crashes before persistence occurs.\
\
